@CC ==================================================================
@CC ECHOMA:MODE - build the MAC TCP echo server
@CC Run as SYSTEM:  @MODE ECHOMA:MODE,,
@CC
@CC Three steps: compile the PLANC socket routines ECHOSH, assemble
@CC the MAC main program ECHOMA, and link both with the SLIB and PLANC
@CC libraries (the same list as ECHOPL:MODE). Then read ECHOSH:LIST for
@CC *** lines, read the MAC lines printed on the terminal for errors,
@CC and check that LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED printed nothing.
@CC
@CC MAC prints its listing on the terminal (TERM) so that an error
@CC shows beside the source line that caused it. Change TERM to 0 for
@CC a quiet build.
@CC
@CC The old outputs are deleted first: a quoted name means CREATE, and
@CC the compiler, MAC and the linker refuse with FILE ALREADY EXISTS if
@CC the file is still there. On the very first build the deletes answer
@CC NO SUCH FILE NAME; that is harmless.
@CC ==================================================================
@DELETE-FILE ECHOSH:LIST
@DELETE-FILE ECHOSH:BRF
@DELETE-FILE ECHOMA:BRF
@DELETE-FILE ECHOMA:PROG
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE ECHOSH:PLNC,"ECHOSH:LIST","ECHOSH"
EXIT
@CC MAC is started from its BPUN file, not with @MAC. On this pack the
@CC reentrant MAC was dumped with start address 0 and runs in a loop
@CC without reading a line (LIST-REENTRANT shows START 0B). ND's own
@CC install sheet (210400B) gives MAC-1415C start -1, restart -3.
@PLACE-BINARY MAC-1415C
@GOTO-USER 177777
)9ASSM ECHOMA:SYMB,TERM,"ECHOMA:BRF"
)9EXIT
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "ECHOMA"
LOAD ECHOMA
LOAD ECHOSH
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD (TCP-IP)SLIB-NRE-1B-B01
LOAD (TCP-IP)SLIB-REE-1B-B01
LOAD MON-CALL-1B-A00
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT
@CC END OF FILE
